            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Created attachment 3937\nAdd fast-path efficiencies to .resetInheritedMethods\n\nLike Bug #19237, this finding is borne out of trying to squeeze down the `loadNamespace()` time for S4 packages (and thereby, in packages depending on S4 packages recursively).\n\n`.resetInheritedMethods()`, called in `.updateMethodsInTable()` when new S4 methods are being registered, needs to reset the cached `MethodWithNext` class for existing methods, if found. The current loop is quadratic because each new package loaded re-checks all previous loaded packages. Mostly, this is not a problem since the N stays small, but for common generics, like `coerce()` / `show()`, this can produce measurable overhead.\n\nHowever, these `MethodWithNext` methods are pretty rare; in the common case that packages are loaded eagerly in an R session (e.g. all required packages are attached up-front with `library()`, and no/few packages are loaded later through `::`), there are none.\n\nTherefore, this patch includes a number of efficient escape valves that avoid running the relatively expensive `is(m, \"MethodWithNext\")`. `isS4()` and `.identC()` checks are much faster and these `next` branches are reached frequently.\n\nThe patch also leverages that methods are in environments, and therefore names are unique, to squeeze out a few extra ms of improvement around removing inherited methods/resetting direct methods.\n\nWe can demonstrate the effect in a particularly slow case with a stack of Bioconductor packages:\n\n```\ntime for ii in {1..20}; do bin/Rscript -e 'for (pkg in c(\"Gviz\", \"ShortRead\", \"raster\", \"timeSeries\", \"MatrixExtra\")) loadNamespace(pkg)'; done\n\n# BEFORE\n# real    6m33.513s\n# user    8m17.133s\n# sys     0m33.026s\n\n# AFTER\n# real    6m19.388s\n# user    8m1.710s\n# sys     0m34.102s\n```\n\nPerhaps more compellingly, we can show it within a single session like so:\n\n```\nlibrary(methods)\ncls <- paste0(\"C\", 1:400)\nsystem.time({\n  for (c_nm in cls) setClass(c_nm)\n  setGeneric(\"g\", function(x) standardGeneric(\"g\"))\n  for (c_nm in cls) setMethod(\"g\", c_nm, function(x) x)\n})\n\n# BEFORE\n#    user  system elapsed \n#   1.333   0.002   1.336\n\n# AFTER\n#    user  system elapsed \n#   0.671   0.000   0.671 \n```\n\nTracking on GitHub: https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/394",
            "bug_id": 19239,
